<!--
  ThreatPulse sitemap.

  Every static page of the product is listed, and the sitemap is advertised in
  robots.txt so crawlers discover it. `lastmod` is stamped at build time by
  scripts/stamp-sitemap.mjs, which runs as part of `npm run build` — a sitemap
  whose dates never move tells a crawler nothing about freshness.

  Individual threat and vulnerability records are deliberately NOT enumerated.
  There are thousands of them, they are superseded wholesale on every
  publication, and they are rendered client-side from an API with no per-record
  HTML — so a crawler would index a near-empty shell for each. The product's
  own pages carry the content; the records are reachable from them.

  The catch-all 404 route is not listed: it must not be indexed.
-->
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
